owel; weak forms of and/to/of/the). Describe only what really happens in this sentence. text is copied exactly from the sentence, soundsLike shows how it sounds (e.g. \"wanna\", \"tur-nit-off\"), note explains in Chinese.\nDo not repeat a word or grammar point across sentences. Keep notes short: about 900 characters at most for one sentence's notes in total, so prefer one example and two collocations.\nIn Chinese text, write digits and Latin letters half-width (4號月台), never full-width, and keep people's names in English as in the sentence."
